      { q:"How did Joshua respond when the people eagerly promised to serve the LORD?", choices:["He immediately made them king's judges","He warned them ye cannot serve the LORD: for he is an holy God; he is a jealous God","He told them to build an altar first","He dismissed the assembly"], a:1, why:"Joshua tested their resolve: Ye cannot serve the LORD: for he is an holy God; he is a jealous God; he will not forgive your transgressions nor your sins." },
      { q:"Why did Joshua open with a long review of Israel's history from Abraham to the conquest?", choices:["To flatter the elders of the tribes","To show that Israel earned the land by its own strength","Because remembering all the LORD had done gives a true basis for choosing to serve Him","Because the people had forgotten their own genealogy"], a:2, why:"The recital ends, I have given you a land for which ye did not labour... now therefore fear the LORD, and serve him in sincerity and in truth." }
